<title>GERMANY: German cartel office approves electricity merger.</title>
<headline>German cartel office approves electricity merger.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1996-11-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>The German federal cartel office on Tuesday approved the merger of two power companies in the Baden-Wuerttemberg region -- Neckarwerke AG (NW) and Technische Werke der Stadt Stuttgart (TWS).</p>
<p>The two companies will merge into a new unit called Neckarwerke Stuttgart AG (NWS), which will supply electricity to the city of Stuttgart, the regional capital, with the exception of the Sindelfingen area.</p>
<p>The federal cartel office said the merger of NW and TWS would not lead to the growth of a monopoly of power supply in the region.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
